# Render static site redirect/rewrite rules for go.referwith50.com.
# Format (Netlify-compatible, what Render's static sites support):
#   <source>  <destination>  <status>
# Status 200 = rewrite (mask): the browser URL bar stays at <source>,
# but the response body is <destination>'s content. Anything else
# (301, 302, ...) is a visible redirect that changes the URL bar.
#
# /login -> fifty-template-dealer.html: a short, memorable URL for the
# staff/admin sign-in page, instead of making people type or link to the
# raw .html filename. Kept as a 200 rewrite (not a redirect) so
# go.referwith50.com/login is the URL people actually see and bookmark.
/login  /fifty-template-dealer.html  200

# Share links (/r/<code>) are served by the API so link-preview crawlers
# (Facebook, iMessage, ...) get tenant-specific Open Graph tags; visitors
# are redirected on to the lead page. See api/src/routes/sharePreview.js.
/r/*  https://five0-platform.onrender.com/r/:splat  200
